{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40435-if-there-is-ever-a-dtf-v20-what-would-you-like-to-see-changed-added","id":40435,"title":"if there is ever a DTF v20 what would you like to see changed/added?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-01T03:02:24-08:00","id":40435,"title":"if there is ever a DTF v20 what would you like to see changed/added?","content":"personally i'd like to see a different lore system. something more versatile, as well as rules(and i mean real rules not the ones we were given that do not even mention how are fallen affected by other splats powers or how they affect them etc.) for crossover. and overall i think than(with a few exceptions) sth similar to devil's due would be a step n the right direction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T11:05:36-08:00","id":40592,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind seeing the realm of Hell or the Archdukes get a further look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T11:12:01-08:00","id":40597,"title":"","content":"would like to see a further explanation on the relationships between the supernatural and the demons, and if the excorism rituals of the werewolves would affect a demon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T23:23:23-08:00","id":40937,"title":"","content":"I'd like it to cease to exist, but baring that I'd like to see Demon mesh better with the other systems with crossover rules even if it's better engineered as a stand alone game. Likewise the other systems could reference Demon more directly as part of the WoD universe. That ship has sailed for some of the systems, but perhaps Wraith and Demon are more directly compatible since the ending events of one system are the impetus for the other. Maybe there's room for some overlap there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:04:14-08:00","id":41228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40435-if-there-is-ever-a-dtf-v20-what-would-you-like-to-see-changed-added?p=40937#post40937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like it to cease to exist, but baring that...</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely don't agree with you here, but I DO understand the sentiment. I have a real love/hate relationship with <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>, and much of that's based on issues you bring up of how poorly the game fits with the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see is a way for the Fallen to be able to interact with the larger World of Darkness in a way that's even internally consistent. By that I mean that <b>Demon</b> references vampires, werewolves, mages and ghosts (Oh my!), but then it leaves the HOW the fallen understand those entities as a huge void. That the Abyss they fled is 'on the other side' of the Underworld is a mad-awesome idea, but then it sorta falls flat even after the discussion of how the Slayers literally CREATED the Underworld. That Lucifer is the one fallen angel who didn't show up in their prison is a wonderful 'red herring' but THEN there's no real connexion between him and Lilith from <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>? Maybe there doesn't need to be any, but it's a dangling thread from what's but into <i>Days of Fire</i>. Then we get all sorts of scary-as-all-fuck stories about the Earthbound as the source material of all kinds of 'demonic' entities, about their cults, about the fell investments they can offer, but then there's nary a head-nod to infernalists like Nephandi, Baali, or to those given over to dark powers like the Wyrm, the Neverborn, etc. It seems like a hole in cosmology.<br /> <br /> ...Now, I know that the above is a little 'ranty' (or perhaps a LOT...), but the thing is that I've always seen tremendous potential in the game. I'd really like to see the rules for creating Apocalyptic Forms, the more full history of the houses, the wider impacts of the demonic condition show up in a <b>D20</b>, all of which appeared in various supplements for the original line, but I'd more want to see a better integration with the World of Darkness. <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> had a weird vibe to it, one that allowed it to affect everything all the while being kept very much to itself, if you know what I mean. If you really read the line, then I'm sure you DO know what I mean, and that's the crux of my love/hate feel towards the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T16:17:14-08:00","id":41379,"title":"","content":"well IIRC i think i read somewhere that a book explaining lilith's connection to lucifer was planned but canceled. could be wrong thought<br /> <br /> also about the abyss it's possible that because it's there because both are outside the&quot;original creation thus it stands to reason that one could go from the underworld there . also the abyss is oblivion. it's also implied that the abyss of the lasombra and maybe even the abyss of the werewolves are the same things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T18:42:02-08:00","id":44601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40435-if-there-is-ever-a-dtf-v20-what-would-you-like-to-see-changed-added?p=41228#post41228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely don't agree with you here, but I DO understand the sentiment. I have a real love/hate relationship with <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>, and much of that's based on issues you bring up of how poorly the game fits with the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see is a way for the Fallen to be able to interact with the larger World of Darkness in a way that's even internally consistent. By that I mean that <b>Demon</b> references vampires, werewolves, mages and ghosts (Oh my!), but then it leaves the HOW the fallen understand those entities as a huge void. That the Abyss they fled is 'on the other side' of the Underworld is a mad-awesome idea, but then it sorta falls flat even after the discussion of how the Slayers literally CREATED the Underworld. That Lucifer is the one fallen angel who didn't show up in their prison is a wonderful 'red herring' but THEN there's no real connexion between him and Lilith from <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>? Maybe there doesn't need to be any, but it's a dangling thread from what's but into <i>Days of Fire</i>. Then we get all sorts of scary-as-all-fuck stories about the Earthbound as the source material of all kinds of 'demonic' entities, about their cults, about the fell investments they can offer, but then there's nary a head-nod to infernalists like Nephandi, Baali, or to those given over to dark powers like the Wyrm, the Neverborn, etc. It seems like a hole in cosmology.<br /> <br /> ...Now, I know that the above is a little 'ranty' (or perhaps a LOT...), but the thing is that I've always seen tremendous potential in the game. I'd really like to see the rules for creating Apocalyptic Forms, the more full history of the houses, the wider impacts of the demonic condition show up in a <b>D20</b>, all of which appeared in various supplements for the original line, but I'd more want to see a better integration with the World of Darkness. <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> had a weird vibe to it, one that allowed it to affect everything all the while being kept very much to itself, if you know what I mean. If you really read the line, then I'm sure you DO know what I mean, and that's the crux of my love/hate feel towards the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with all of this. But there's a bit more to it than that. Not only do I feel like Demon doesn't fit, but it was the part in a continuing line of very transparent pushes to make money off of a popular trends in franchising. The books came out at a faster pace and more rushed and I for one can tell the writing suffered greatly for it. White-Wolf grew too large too fast and some of the earlier systems were neglected as writers and developers juggled many projects from different systems and had to prioritize their attention depending on the deadlines. It lost the depth of culture that the Second edition era seemed to have. (And in some cases they didn't even bother finishing off the second edition versions of books. Boggan Kithbook and Guildbooks anyone?) Revised and the new systems that were added post 1999 one and all have a different feel to them. Rushing headlong, literally towards the end times. I would actually prefer to play a version of In Nomine set in World of Darkness with all its detail and cosmology than play Demon: the Fallen as it's presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  typos 01-07-2014, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T06:35:23-08:00","id":44865,"title":"","content":"Heh. Back about a year or two before Demon came out, I remember attending a Game Con that hosted a Vampire/In Nomine crossover LARP. It was\u2026 interesting. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d certainly appreciate a Revised Edition for Demon that approaches it from the perspective of \u201coh, look at that; the world didn\u2019t end after all! Now what?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:21:27-08:00","id":45053,"title":"","content":"I unabashedly love Demon, but it can be ridiculously clunky. I don't think we've ever managed to play it with the right rules. Primarily, I'd like to see High Torment Lore effects come up more often, because the systems in the core and the player's guide don't really mean much to the average PC, unless you're gaining Torment like nobody's business.<br /> <br /> I'd also like a deeper system for how True Names get strewn around when you use your powers. That's one of the best parts of the setting, but it's probably the vaguest part of the system.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to the Demon Translation Guide for Demon: The Descent/Fallen. I'd like to see how it runs in NWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T08:40:25-07:00","id":604745,"title":"","content":"Would be nice to see more details for jumping between hosts, and I'd personally prefer if they did away with the &quot;OUR RELIGION IS TRUTH!!1one&quot; and left it more ambiguous or otherwise included options for it such as &quot;what if God didn't create but rather just stumbled upon the place and decided to add his own touches&quot; or something along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T09:54:14-07:00","id":604781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">personally i'd like to see a different lore system. something more versatile</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on that...always feel Lore to be a little limited for the so called &quot;sum of all secrets of the Creation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Conceptually they're good, but they act more like superpowers than knowledg...until you get to use rituals...and even then, one misses the skill to do more immediate things that shouldn't need hours of casting with Lore, like reading in many languages in a similar way as you can identify a different spoken language.<br /> <br /> Also, I would like that the text explores the possibility of playing the Fallen before 1999. After all, Fallen could be invoked in a human host before the 6th Maelstrom, and thus Demon could be played before that (if rarely).<br /> <br /> Oh, and crossover stuff it's always nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T12:07:08-07:00","id":604893,"title":"","content":"I'd want to see a DtF20 that divorces itself entirely from the original metaplot reason for them walking the earth after all these years, since we're officially in &quot;metaplot neutral&quot; territory nowadays. Either give them a purely internal reason for only escaping &quot;right now&quot;, or have change it so they've always been able to cross over into the earthly realm if the circumstances are just right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T12:22:58-07:00","id":604900,"title":"","content":"I would want house books. I want to see expanded lores, house specific lore options, more lores that were made after the fallen returned to earth.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T22:23:52-07:00","id":605299,"title":"","content":"Good crossover rules and a more versatyle Lore system, for sure.<br /> <br /> Personaly, I'm not happy with the system for devouring other demons. I'm not sure if it is a good idea to begin with, and surely not the way it is now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T00:59:37-07:00","id":605385,"title":"","content":"It's just a pet peeve of mine, but for summoning, an explanation if there are demons below the Fell Knight Rank left in Hell to summon out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T08:20:51-07:00","id":605617,"title":"","content":"I want more consistency in the writing; I get so confused about various infernal ranks like Fell Knights and Barons because we see demons in human hosts with them when we're then told that they can't be.<br /> <br /> I also want the mechanics to be rather dramatically overhauled. Inspiration taken from the Devil's Due book for mechanics is always a positive in my opinion, but not a verbatim replication either; those need some work too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:40:11-07:00","id":605655,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind an explanation on Rank. In the summoning section we keep hearing how the sight a Demon of higher Rank being summoned out of Hell makes your character take a Courage roll. What could a Demon do to increase his Rank, and what are the mechanics of Rank that create its spiritual aura?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:05:54-07:00","id":606587,"title":"","content":"I've posted this on the KotE thread, but will bring it up here as well.<br /> <br /> I would like Demon, KotE, and Mummy (and maybe Risen) to get merged into a single game about clawing, crawling, or buying your way out of hell. (Or at least the afterlife.)<br /> <br /> Of course, it would require some overhaul of all three, but honestly, I think it would be a stronger overall product than any of them started as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:46:30-07:00","id":607266,"title":"","content":"Isn't in the spirit of the 20th editions to actualy change things so drasticaly, and Demon doesn't have anything to do with the hells of KotE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T02:38:31-07:00","id":607565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40435-if-there-is-ever-a-dtf-v20-what-would-you-like-to-see-changed-added?p=607266#post607266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't in the spirit of the 20th editions to actualy change things so drasticaly, and Demon doesn't have anything to do with the hells of KotE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've said about the same. Maybe some one more imaginative than myself can come up with ways to tweak the products for a line that doesn't include the 'end times', while maintaining a degree of respect for the cultures involved. <br /> <br /> I think if there were only one WoD, we'd be good for a big overhaul. But with 2, how far from the original can OP stray before alienating the audience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:51:21-07:00","id":608410,"title":"","content":"Te thing is, a big overhaul isn't intende and shouldn't be. Some lines can get more work than others because they had some specific issues, specialy on rules. Demon deserves some special attention because it never had a second edition, so a lot of 1st ed common issues are found. As Changeling probably will have, since it desperately needed a Revised ed and it never came.<br /> <br /> But that's all. The 20th games aren't about rewright the setting in any way. To do that is counterproductive for the very objective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T15:37:07-07:00","id":608513,"title":"","content":"Well, yes and no. The settings can be <i>updated</i> to account for real-world developments that have occurred since the game's last edition (e.g., Mummy's picture of the Middle East is badly out of date) or even merely for the passage of time: the first edition of <b>Hunter</b> relied heavily on the notion that the Imbued are a <i>brand new phenomenon</i> that nobody has had a chance to come to terms with; how do things change when there's a whole generation of young adults who were born after the Imbuement phenomenon began? <br /> <br /> Also, I wouldn't be opposed to the various \u201clatter-day games\u201d (the ones that lean heavily on the Ghost Storm for their very existence) each getting an Appendix that's essentially a \u201cpre-Ghost Storm Shard\u201d: the Imbued recast as an alternate take on True Faith for \u201cYear of the Hunter\u201d-style hunters (essentially, a modern-day counterpart to \u201cDark Ages: Inquisitor\u201d); mummies in the style of \u201cMummy Second Edition\u201d implemented using the rules of \u201cMummy: the Resurrection\u201d; and taking a page from \u201cDevil\u2019s Due\u201d to present something not unlike the Fallen before the gates of the Abyss were cracked open. No more than an Appendix, though, and clearly presented as a variant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T17:15:59-07:00","id":608634,"title":"","content":"Since there are the metaplot-free aspect, they should probably give advise on using them before, right after and long after the escape from Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:06:09-07:00","id":609006,"title":"","content":"I got a little suggestion for a few things<br /> <br /> To make lores more attuned to spheres (concidering that Elohims are the Builders and shapers of the creation)<br /> <br /> A new Merit/Flaw: Animal Host (See Mr Pickles) <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WAkjM0UBf4c\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WAkjM0UBf4c</a><br /> <br /> the defect of &quot;Known Angelic Name.&quot; if you have an demon with a very popular name, you will hear humans mentioning you ALL THE TIME! you wont be able to think straight (Examples: raziel, azrael, or any angel name that appears on mass media)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Host Awarness (flaw)</span></b></i></span><br /> <br /> Sometimes they come back, and sometimes they take over what it belongs to them<br /> Yes, i know that the host is technically dead and his soul is pushed away..but what if a little piece of the host is Aware somewhere deep within the chambers of the human body taken over by the Demonic Being?. One can imagine the horrors that you can witness as a &quot;Backseat passenger.&quot; This would add a new mechanic to the game.<br /> Fight for Control<br /> Every time your Demon doesnt acts according to the Human Character of the Host (For example doing things that would go against the values of the original Mortal: threating the lives of the ones close to you, use your lores to corrupt to Sin to the ones you love, destroy your own personal life etc...) the original Host (Which we will call The True Will), will be able to fight the demon from within.<br /> <br /> Each time the Fallen acts against his primal human nature within the boundries of the human host, he will get not only suspicious. but he will add a new stat called &quot;Desperation.&quot; similar to torment.<br /> <br /> Desperation works similar to the Wraith's Angst (Hell. its even a carbon sort of copy of the Shadow play).<br /> <br /> Each time the Demon attempts to do something against the host original values, he will roll his correspondant Virtue against the True Will's Desesperation (Which starts at level 3). If the demon wins, he will mantain full control of the possession no questions answered..<br /> <br /> IF the True Will wins, he will start earning temporal Desperation. These can be used to do use &quot;Glimpses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Glimpses are manifestations of the true sinister nature, a sort of &quot;Cry for Help&quot; from the inside.<br /> Example of Glimpses are<br /> Manifest an Apocaliptic Form (high level)<br /> Manifest a Lore (high Level)<br /> Speak in Tongues while Sleeping (low Level)<br /> Forcing the Damage (to make a demon actually feel pain when he is close to a holy object, even if he has low torment, high level)<br /> Book of Blood (To be able to make wounds in the demon's host body with messages to anyone outside. high level)<br /> Levitation (high level)<br /> Cold Spots (high level)<br /> Backwards Messages in Technology (low level)<br /> Mind Blasts (for the human host to be able to move objects at a max of Strg 1 and dex 1, low level)<br /> Idle Hands (for the True Will to be able to manipulate the Hand of the Demon upholding the Possession, High Level)<br /> Partial Message (for the True Will to be able to physically manifest for a number of turns equal to his permanent Desesperation. High level)<br /> Scared Animals and atract the vermin (Low level)<br /> Proyect Nightmare to a Human (High Level)<br /> Manipulation of the Shell (High Level, this involves little manipulations such as making the Demon's body not be able to blink. or manipulate the heartbeat in erratical ways, make the human body to blink with lizard like eyes, make him loose his teeths etc... This WONT CAUSE THE HOST'S BODY TO DIE. THEY ARE PURELY AESTHETHIC CHANGES)<br /> Inhumane Urges (forcing the Body Host to feed of non common meals such as bugs, dirt, nails etc.. technically speaking, nothing that would harm the body host but raise a lot of red flags)<br /> <br /> How can a demon defend himself from Desesperations and True Will?<br /> One: IF the demon's torment is higher than the desesperation level, he can keep control over the True Will through sheer Fear. Though, this will make the True Will to act more reckless and trying to manifest more and more to warn his loved ones<br /> Two: Acceptance, For the Fallen to be able to Comute with the True Will and manage to go through their lives and accept Death (Example: a low torment fallen would reach within his own mind and soul for the True Will and show him how he is trying to make things better, to accept the Goodness of one to protect or to say &quot;Leave it to me, ill protect your loved ones. you may rest in peace)<br /> Three: Binding Rituals, To be able to use rituals related to the Lore of Humanity in order to force the True Will fully bound and tied up (But...if it manages to set itself free through his own personal Desperation, he might be able to fuck the demon back and make people aware of the danger within itself).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Desesperation Mechanic:<br /> <br /> I talked a lot about these, so. How would it work?<br /> This stat goes from 1 to 10, starting at the same level of torment that the demon has.<br /> IF, the demon has this flaw (or the DM wishes to apply this mechanic). each time the fallen does a horrible inhumane act that attempts against the host's primordial nature, beliefs about values or things/people he cared about. The True Will might fight the Fallen to try and Stop it (or to give enough hints for it to be exorcised and reclaim the Flesh again...if an exorcism works, its up to the ST)<br /> <br /> Each time the demon acts against his Host' nature, he must roll for the Virtue VS the Desperation. The biggest the threat to the Original Host (or True Will), the lower the difficulty.<br /> If the ammount of successes of the Demon are Higher than the ones rolled by the True Will, the demon remains control and nothing happends.<br /> <br /> If the true will has more successes than the Demon, he may add those successes to his Desesperation Pool.<br /> The desperation might be spend to.<br /> -use a Low Level Glimpse<br /> -activate a High Level Glimpse (Costs 3 points of Desperation).<br /> -Increase the difficulty to all rolls (except for Damage rolls) <br /> Desperation can not be lowered by any other way thats not by Spending Desperation points.<br /> <br /> <br /> The whole idea of the thing is to create a new antagonist, a human trying to reach outside like a miner trapped on a mine. Knowing that someone or something is wearing his flesh and trying to find a way out by Not being Sutil. They want to break the mask of the demon so they can be released from the dak being's grasps.<br /> <br /> I just came up with the whole idea..i know theres A LOT of thingsto be fixed but what do you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:50:24-07:00","id":609077,"title":"","content":"I was thinking On a new sort of metaplot<br /> <br /> Im typing from a phone so bear with me, using the speak to type<br /> <br /> The beginning the creator was there. The creator divided in several others each one is perfect that's her she decided to create a new world a new life so she allowed the parts shards this create everything<br /> <br /> Each shard was unique, shard had a vision about what the world should be about how things were to become on how things went to be<br /> <br /> H should have had his whole name which shark has its own story to tell about how the world was made but the ligh light on the creation of everything for the church are made Elohim Angel messengers builders of reality of the reality. Each piece of the creator wanted to use to create some pieces of names that have blessed upon this day some other pieces have been forgotten to the sounds of time I'm so even have been demoted to become angel of them own<br /> <br /> The idea is to say that there was one thing that one being the divided self into multiple pieces it's suggested or maybe him that each piece is supposed to become a god of some sorts either be the queen of them the Pantheon the Egyptians Pantheon etcetera etcetera<br /> <br /> they do is that every every religion in the 20 world of darkness setting is setting , is working.<br /> because everybody's right and everybody's wrong<br /> <br /> <br /> Know how to explain the return of the fallen ones? I've been thinking a lot about some ideas from me the Ascension as the possibility. <br /> <br /> Humans were able to pierce through the abyss in order to break the gates. its been handed in the world of darkness there's demons but not like the ones we know the following these demons that we know from the wilderness are spirits from the Umbra but in the human's small perception they see them us this massive being , demons show the beliefs of the end of the world of the rupture of dark times mainly bad energies in the world and negative thinking and the faith that the end of the world is coming allows us to break free through this world why it didn't happen before well that's an interesting question what is the dip what if every time a message civilization believes in the end of the world scenario a group of the following worms are able to manifest in this world I mean every time some massive cult or religion that leaves in the morning energy sword at the hell will come to earth what is everytimes massive groups with a lot of faith believe in an Apocalypse Scenario manage to pierce through the gates of the abyss?<br /> This will allow the flocking of some demons there could be a couple of demons engine warms in the world this could be from the medieval times see The Devil's Due to live in war world 1 &amp; 2 or noun with the author assume things like the Westboro Baptist Church or the whole a deal that the rapture is coming more and more fallen to break free from the jail","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T23:57:41-07:00","id":614655,"title":"","content":"A bit more balance for the houses / lore would be quite nice (some houses / lores were a bit overpowered compared to others (devils as example)). <br /> <br /> <br /> Also an update on the apocalyptic forms. The build your own in the storyteller guide was quite nice but with only 16 pts it was almost impossible to use the freedom given (as example I had houseruled back then that it was increased by 1 point each the more powerful the demon grew). As you needed 4 high and 4 low torment powers (aka 8 pts.....if you didnt have at least 4 one point powers then ouch).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T23:57:56-07:00","id":616037,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the build your own was a good feature, but needs urgent improvement.<br /> <br /> I won't talk about balance of Houses/Lore for now because I want to see the system for Lores rewritten to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T15:23:43-07:00","id":619508,"title":"","content":"I want a book that shows how the fallen's outlook changes when they find themselves in possession of bodies that subscribed to different religions such as Buddhism, Norse mythology, so on and so forth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:11:37-07:00","id":619569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40435-if-there-is-ever-a-dtf-v20-what-would-you-like-to-see-changed-added?p=619508#post619508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a book that shows how the fallen's outlook changes when they find themselves in possession of bodies that subscribed to different religions such as Buddhism, Norse mythology, so on and so forth</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were going to make a new core, that should probably be one of the first things in it, in the first chapter of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T10:05:29-07:00","id":620215,"title":"","content":"I would also like to see how demons look through the lenses of other religions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:01:43-07:00","id":627000,"title":"","content":"I would like for them to Retconn either the Earthbound background &quot;Mastery&quot; (which is an innate Earthbound ability--i.e., any Earthbound can have it--and the background is only a reflection of any given demon's ability to use it) which is found in the Earthbound book; <i><b>OR</b></i> the Ritual &quot;Volcano<i>&quot; </i>from <i>Houses of the Fallen</i>. The combination of these powers (frankly it's not far fetched for an Earthbound to have Lore of Earth 5; Lore of Flames 2; and this Ritual) is <i>devastating.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Mastery</i> (per <i>Earthbound</i>, pg. 85) works like so:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As well as performing evocations as normal, you can choose to enhance an evocation after successfully rolling for its effect. Only characters with at least one dot in the Mastery Background can enhance evoca- tions in this fashion.<br /> To enhance an evocation, increasing its range, area of affect, number of targets or other such vari- ables, the player spends Faith after making a successful evocation roll. Each point of Faith spent increases a specific aspect of the evocation tenfold: 10 times the range, affecting up to 10 targets instead of one, etc. Spending two points increases the aspect 100 times, spending three points increases it 1,000 times and so on. If multiple aspects of the evocation could be enhanced, each must be enhanced with Faith points separately. </div> </div> </div>Thus, for every level in the background <i>Mastery</i> (yes, <i>Background</i>--not a separate power), an Earthbound may spend a point of Faith to increase one effect of an invocation by a factor of 10.<br /> <br /> <i>Volcano</i> (per <i>Houses of the Fallen</i>, pg. 83) works like so:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>System:</b> Roll Str+Surv. If the roll succeeds, a volcano grows form the ritual's sigil, a massive cone of earth that spouts molten lava for a number of <i>hours</i> equal to the successes gained. The lava moves slowly in an ever-expanding radius and causes great damage to the surrounding area. The Ankida cannon control the spread of lava once the volcano begins to erupt. Each hour the radius affected increases by a number of yards equal to 100 times the successes of the ritual. (So with three successes, the lava would spread out another 300 yards each hour.) Almost all objects in the area will be destroyed, including buildings and vehicles, once the come into contact with the lava. Any character in contact with the lava suffers a number of lethal health levels each turn equal to the successes rolled, which cannot be soaked by armor. When the ritual's effect ends, the volcano crumbles in on itself and the lava cools unnaturally quickly, leaving behind a lake of coarse, brittle stone about an hour later.<br /> <br /> <b>Torment: </b>The high-Torment version of this ritual produces lava streaming with corruption and radioactive toxins, jetting from the volcano high into the air. The corrupt lava expands much faster than normal. The radius affected increases by a <i>mile</i> each hour, regardless of the successes rolled for the evocation. When the ritual ends, the lava stays hot and will take several days to cool. Furthermore, its corrupt nature poisons the earth beneath it, rendering it permanently toxic and polluted. </div> </div> </div>SO, let's say an Earthbound with Master 5 (again, this is background--any Earthbound can have it), and this Ritual (which I will grant you is not a &quot;main book&quot; power) casts the <i>high-Torment </i>version of the power and spends five Faith points to increase the evocation to the max. That would mean that with a single success, the toxic evil lava would go out to a radius of 100,000 miles in every direction <i>in a single hour</i>. However, the Circumference of the Earth is scarcely more than 24,000 miles. So basically we have a hypersonic wave of radioactive lava sweeping over the planet like four separate times in an hour.<br /> <br /> I get that no Storyteller should ever allow this (if nothing else, some Deus Ex Machina like Lucifer should show up to stop it)... but certainly it should not be so damn easy to bring about the end of the entire planet. One Ritual (which requires only Lore of Earth 5 and Lore of Fire 2, and obviously knowledge of the ritual itself), and a Background (which even at 4 is still DEVASTATING to the planet) should not be all that it takes to turn the planet into a fiery, radioactive heap.<br /> <br /> Just sayin' s'all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 08-14-2015, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:28:21-07:00","id":627049,"title":"","content":"Granted, It is a &quot;bit&quot; over, but...<br /> <br /> It is also simple to correct, if not already corrected.<br /> <br /> Are you sure that <i>Mastery</i> can affect <i>Rituals</i>?<br /> <br /> Not saying they can't, I'm not sure, really. But if they do, just change to &quot;do not&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}